    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97120" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρᾰτηγ-ίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, fem. Adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of the general</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκηνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					4.19.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύλαι</span> the door or entrance
				<i>of the general's tent</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				49
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς ς</span>.
			<i>flag</i>-ship, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.84
			</span></i> (pl.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.11
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ς</span>. alone, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.92
			</span></i>; at Rome, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. σπεῖραι</span>
			<i>cohortes praetoriae</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				39
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				3.45
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάξεις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
				Subst., fem. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατηγός</span>, <i>female commander</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				835
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				870
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				235
			</span></i>.</div>
